WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:04.300
This is the second son of 
a mold-starter business owner,

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.480
who just started at the Agricultural 
University this spring,

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.980
Sawaki Souemon Tadayasu-kun.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:13.550
He has the ability to see 
microbes with the naked eye.

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:10.730
A. oryzae

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:12.990
A.   aceti

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:14.990
Amazing, isn't it?

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.040
Oh, man! We're surrounded!

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:01.700
Moyashimon

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.310
Microbes, Microbes Everywhere

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.560
Sawaki-kun and the others don't 
seem to be coming today.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:25.110
They've been dropping in frequently,

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:28.080
but they're not official 
seminar students yet.

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:31.390
Besides, the first-years 
are probably busy

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:32.880
with their required courses.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.340
Oh, right. 
Still planting that rice, eh?

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.840
It's also that time of year again.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.210
Yes.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:49.160
Anyone who doesn't go into 
the paddy will be marked absent!

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:52.350
Rice planting is mandatory 
for all first-years!

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:56.880
Of the 3.5 million 
farmers in Japan today,

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.240
two million are over the age of 65.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:02.370
The future of farming 
depends on the strength of

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:03.450
young people like you!

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:04.240
Work hard!

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.860
Why are we planting rice 
by hand in a square field?

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:11.730
Isn't there a machine for this?

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:12.950
You said it.

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:16.130
Rice planting is something you 
take leave from school to do.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:18.000
Schools still allow days off

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.130
for rice planting in your hometown?

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.100
Where I come from, we only planted

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.140
rice for grade school projects.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.370
There were weeds everywhere, 
and even leeches!

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:28.800
It was awful!

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:31.050
Now that you mention it,

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:33.810
even the furrows look well-kept.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:35.150
No microbes, either!

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:38.770
They must be keeping them 
cleared out with herbicides.

00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:41.730
Is it okay to use chemicals 
even on the furrows?

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:43.070
It is an agricultural university.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:45.430
I'm sure they're careful 
about the amounts they use.

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:46.230
Probably.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:55.570
Free at last...

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:57.660
Man, it's evening already.

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:00.760
So, are you two going to see 
the professor again today?

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.310
It's not like I hang 
out with that professor

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:05.040
every day because I want to.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:08.760
Every time we see him, 
he makes us eat weird stuff.

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.640
Like kiviak...

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:12.520
and hongeohoe.

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:19.100
Hey, there!

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.780
Are you digging something up again?

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:24.770
I had some menma buried under 
this furrow to ferment.

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:26.910
I thought I'd dig them up today.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.230
Menma?

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.290
You mean the bamboo shoots 
served on top of ramen?

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:33.360
Fermenting Chinese bamboo shoots

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.540
underground softens them.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:38.730
Fall is really the best 
season for them, though.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:40.750
That's fermented, too?

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.160
It certainly is.

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:44.680
The menma I make are delicious!

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:46.470
Now that you mention it,

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:48.870
there are a lot of soil microbes here.

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:52.140
There were practically none 
around the rice paddy.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.640
The paddy you were in is specifically 
for herbicide testing.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:58.910
It's maintained perfectly 
through the wisdom of science,

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:01.840
which reduces the costs and 
labor required for mowing.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:04.150
But this paddy is fallow.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:06.410
The soil microbes here now are

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:09.160
boosting the strength 
of the weakened soil.

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:12.830
The furrows here are covered in weeds.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:16.020
They aren't weeds at all.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:18.330
These furrows are full of treasures.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:24.080
There's Jersey cudweed, 
bird's-eye, dandelions...

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:27.670
The flowering plants on these 
dikes give farms their color.

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:29.680
Even the seven spring 
herbs are originally

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:32.100
found on the paths along 
furrows like these.

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:36.360
What's in that beaker?

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:38.100
Hm? Oh...

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:42.560
Kawahama-kun was studying 
earthworms in the lab.

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:45.390
When I said I was coming out here,

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:47.100
he asked me to bring some back.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:50.430
Along with soil microbes,

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:53.710
earthworms are very important 
for enriching soil.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:57.330
Their feces act as fertilizer, 
and they even till the soil.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:59.260
They're very beneficial creatures.

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:02.730
The leader in the field 
of earthworm research

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:04.920
was the man known for the theory 
of evolution, Charles Darwin.

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:08.150
Earthworms are remarkable 
creatures that

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:10.930
support the very foundations 
of Earth's ecology.

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:14.400
Now then, let's get back to the lab

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:17.080
and raise a toast to the 
wild herbs of the furrows!

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:19.720
Professor, as I've told you before,

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:22.050
we're still underage.

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:26.050
Come, Researcher Misato!

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:28.450
What is it, Researcher Kawahama?

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:32.610
This is the epidermal mucus of the 
earthworm, Researcher Misato.

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:35.450
I don't understand, 
Researcher Kawahama!

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:39.460
And these are deep fried 
earthworms, Researcher Misato!

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:43.460
They don't look tasty at all, 
Researcher Kawahama!

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:45.770
Would you like to look, too?

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:47.360
Researcher Hasegawa!

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:52.920
Shut up!

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:54.350
Don't bring me down to your level!

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:59.600
Professor, I honestly don't 
believe we need these two!

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:03.150
They have nothing to talk 
about but sake and bugs!

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:05.090
What are you talking about?!

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:07.210
Don't underestimate the power of bugs!

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:09.280
It was earthworms that cured my cold!

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:10.700
It's said that the broth

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.660
boiled from earthworms 
can reduce a fever!

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:15.870
Earthworms are the dragons of the soil!

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.990
Their power is immense!

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:20.910
I couldn't care less!

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:22.310
No matter what the professor says,

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:24.730
I still haven't accepted you two!

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:27.090
Here, Kawahama-kun, for you.

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:29.550
Thank you!

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:32.980
Why, Professor?!

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:35.550
Well, it's nice and lively 
with them here, isn't it?

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:38.190
But, what a bind...

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:41.540
I don't have enough snacks 
for a party of seven.

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:43.660
Hasegawa-kun...

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:44.580
Yes?

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:47.490
We could use some vegetables.

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:48.570
It's spring, after all.

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:54.530
If I recall, Farm B1 
has spring vegetables.

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:56.190
Spring vegetables, eh?

00:07:56.190 --> 00:07:58.080
Asparagus sounds good.

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:00.450
Sawaki.

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:05.210
This is Farm B1.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:08.710
If you go straight there and 
back, it'll take 30 minutes.

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:11.000
It's all outdoor, 
so getting in is a breeze.

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:14.970
W-Wait just a minute...

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:19.190
You'd better pull this off!

00:08:19.190 --> 00:08:21.480
Don't worry. It'll be easy.

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:23.330
Are you kidding me?

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:25.870
I've never stolen vegetables before.

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:28.040
Well, we're under orders 
from the professor.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:29.550
It should be okay, right?

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:33.170
When I know I'm about 
to do something bad,

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:35.070
suddenly it seems like there 
are more people around.

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:39.240
There are a lot of lights 
on for this time of night.

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:43.500
Is it okay to make them steal?

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:45.700
It's fine.

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:49.000
Farm B1 was created 
just for this event.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:51.000
Event?

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.890
What is this all about?

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:03.350
I have no idea.

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:06.720
There are thieves all over the place!

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:08.520
They all look like first-years.

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:10.850
Your club sent you here, too?

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:12.860
Yeah, I don't get it.

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:15.030
They just told me out of 
the blue to get vegetables.

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:16.720
There were first-years from a lot of

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:18.140
different clubs at Farm B1.

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:19.960
Sawaki...

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:21.780
I think this is something like

00:09:21.780 --> 00:09:24.500
a game involving the whole school.

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:25.880
Yeah.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:28.310
I've had it with being dragged 
into these stupid farces

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:29.600
and humiliating myself.

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:31.500
Hey, look.

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:35.250
According to the map, 
Farm B7 has spring vegetables, too.

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:37.830
You're right. And it's closer.

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:39.430
I say we go for B7.

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:42.890
Farm B7 also has spring 
vegetables, but it's a trap.

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:44.390
A trap?

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:47.220
Yep. Farm B7 is just for

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:49.970
testing highly concentrated herbicides.

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:51.480
Nothing there is for eating.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:59.700
Warning! 
Currently Testing 
Highly Concentrated Herbicides

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:54.990
There used to be a lot of poor students

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:57.460
who broke in there to steal vegetables,

00:09:57.460 --> 00:09:59.700
and couldn't see the warning 
signs because it was dark.

00:10:00.310 --> 00:10:03.260
So, a few years ago, 
they turned it into an event

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:06.330
using first-years to warn people 
that stealing can be dangerous.

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:11.120
Go!

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:22.160
Intruders in Farm B7!

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:24.080
All forces advance immediately!

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:25.920
It's begun.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:30.030
I wonder which first-years got 
caught cheating this time.

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:32.720
By the way, last year 
it was me and Misato.

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:33.610
I see...

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:36.370
The guys who catch them seem to

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:38.150
have fun ambushing them, too.

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:40.700
Hell, in spring, 
all the clubs hang around

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:43.820
until nighttime every day 
just waiting for this event.

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:51.700
They ran that way! After them!

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:00.310
Why?!

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:03.850
I don't know, but they're 
definitely chasing us!

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:04.930
Let's hide!

00:11:17.270 --> 00:11:18.730
I see them! Over there!

00:11:18.730 --> 00:11:20.020
Get them!

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:27.870
Oh, man! We're surrounded!

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:29.500
Give yourselves up.

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:32.420
I guess this is it.

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:34.420
You...

00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:38.980
...vegetable thieves!

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:43.150
Why are they all smiling?

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:52.810
Notice and Warning of Herbicide Testing

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:52.810
This 
Year's 
Offenders

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:52.810
Agricultural Dept.  1st Year  
Sawaki Tadayasu-kun

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:52.810
Agricultural Dept.  1st Year  
Yuuki Kei-kun

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:52.810
You two will be famous now.

00:11:53.550 --> 00:11:56.550
The people in our class 
really let us have it.

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:59.210
I'll get some copies for 
you later as a memento.

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:00.320
No thanks.

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:03.690
What's wrong, Sawaki? You feeling sick?

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:06.740
Just a case of the runs.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:09.110
Maybe the milk you drank 
in livestock yesterday

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:10.330
didn't agree with you?

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:14.070
I've had trouble with 
milk since I was little.

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:15.460
Are you gonna be okay?

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:17.370
You have orientation next, don't you?

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:23.430
Are you all on board 
the wagons by class?

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:24.840
Yes.

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:28.850
Okay, everyone watch 
class 1's tractor here.

00:12:29.650 --> 00:12:32.800
One of the biggest themes 
in modern agricultural research

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:34.480
is environmental issues.

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:38.050
This bio-tractor is a prototype 
with an engine designed

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:41.860
by one of our senior bio students 
with corporate cooperation.

00:12:42.390 --> 00:12:44.410
It's a biomass engine that derives

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:47.060
its propulsive power from 
heat generated by burning

00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:49.160
rice husks instead of fossil fuel.

00:12:49.670 --> 00:12:51.970
This university's really 
doing it right.

00:12:51.970 --> 00:12:53.660
Class 1 is so lucky.

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:56.400
Everyone watch. 
We're going to start it up.

00:12:57.470 --> 00:12:59.260
Go for it, guys.

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:01.670
Right! We'll show those first-years!

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:09.430
Wow, there's no smoke!

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:12.080
Huh?

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:13.230
The wagon...

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:15.630
It doesn't have the 
power to pull a wagon?

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:19.100
I guess that's cutting 
edge technology for you.

00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:21.520
The upperclassmen look 
thrilled, though.

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:24.420
Yeah!!

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:23.550
Oh, it stopped.

00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:30.310
So in the end,

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:33.060
class 1 had to be pulled 
by a regular tractor, too.

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:35.280
And did you see that eco-car?

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:36.810
They were all pushing it home.

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:39.530
I thought orientation

00:13:39.530 --> 00:13:42.090
would just be a speech 
in the lecture hall,

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:44.780
but it looks like we'll be 
touring the campus all morning.

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:48.390
And lunch will be a buffet 
prepared by the upperclassmen.

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:51.970
Sort of feels like our college 
life has finally begun.

00:13:53.070 --> 00:13:54.600
Actually...

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:57.100
I feel like we're being 
hauled off to market.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:58.850
Wanna sing Donna Donna?

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:07.490
What a nice breeze.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:10.610
I wonder if Sawaki's stomach is okay.

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:12.740
Yeah...

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:15.750
There'll be some hard 
stops on their tour.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:23.250
Livestock

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:19.180
Okay, everyone draw a straw.

00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:20.780
The red straw is the winner,

00:14:20.780 --> 00:14:23.250
so whoever draws red will represent 
the class in this study.

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:25.880
What's he calling a "study"?

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:27.330
I'm tired of this.

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:29.130
I wanna go home.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:31.720
Whew, I didn't get red!

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:32.770
Here, Sawaki.

00:14:39.470 --> 00:14:40.650
It's red...

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:47.160
You insert your arm into 
the anus like this

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:48.920
to check the size of 
the ovarian follicles

00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:51.530
and determine when the cow is ready 
for artificial insemination.

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:54.130
Don't make any loud noises.

00:14:54.130 --> 00:14:56.490
If the cow gets spooked, 
she'll take your arm off.

00:14:58.270 --> 00:15:01.150
Isn't that one of the guys 
who got caught yesterday?

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:03.290
There was a big fuss over him 
at the entrance ceremony, too.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.110
You may think this has nothing to do

00:15:06.110 --> 00:15:07.940
with any of you in the 
agricultural department,

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:10.480
but everything is linked somehow 
in Agricultural University,

00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:12.510
and you will have to work 
with livestock eventually,

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:13.990
so be sure to remember this.

00:15:14.730 --> 00:15:17.990
Does that mean I'll have 
to do this someday, too?

00:15:17.990 --> 00:15:19.310
What's it like, Sawaki?

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:22.550
I-It's warm...

00:15:22.550 --> 00:15:24.810
and every now and then, 
something moves...

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:27.620
I've seen people do it on TV...

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:31.820
but seeing it in person 
is pretty intense.

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:34.670
If we were to express agriculture in a word,

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:36.650
it would be "broad."

00:15:36.650 --> 00:15:38.160
From garbage bins that turn garbage

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:40.170
into mulch through the 
work of microorganisms

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:43.010
to microwave ovens that 
can make fried chicken

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:44.330
using hot steam instead of oil,

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:45.990
they all trace back to agriculture.

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:48.230
Um, how long is he 
going to keep talking?

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:50.590
My stomach hurts...

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:56.850
Stew                     Curry

00:15:57.830 --> 00:15:59.350
The first-years are at it.

00:15:59.870 --> 00:16:02.200
Looks like it's lunch time.

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:05.100
I hope no one's found out 
about Sawaki-kun's ability.

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:08.630
It's hard to say. He's pretty stupid.

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:11.280
This year's lunch has been prepared by

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.220
our upperclassmen from 
the livestock department.

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:14.240
There's a lot to choose from,

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:15.780
so take whichever you 
like and have a seat.

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:19.540
Don't eat until everyone is seated!

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:24.330
It's hopeless.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:26.640
My stomach hurts too much to eat.

00:16:26.640 --> 00:16:27.950
Hey!

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:30.200
You're not supposed to eat yet!

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:31.300
I'm not.

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:34.320
Besides, we're college students.

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:36.930
There's no need for everyone 
to start eating together.

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:39.310
What did you guys get?

00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:41.000
I got salad and bread.

00:16:45.510 --> 00:16:48.560
You've already been elbow-deep 
in cow dung with an upset stomach.

00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:49.650
Why did you get curry?

00:16:50.390 --> 00:16:52.570
I can't eat raw stuff.

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:56.110
Apparently, even the mayonnaise 
was made by the livestock department.

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:57.370
Looks great, doesn't it?

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:07.130
Time to brew!

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:10.130
Everyone! Don't eat this!

00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:12.960
What's going on?

00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:13.730
Dunno.

00:17:13.730 --> 00:17:14.510
Let's eat.

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:16.030
Don't eat this!

00:17:16.030 --> 00:17:17.760
There's something really bad in it!

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:19.680
We're gonna brew! Brew!

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:23.120
Brew!

00:17:23.740 --> 00:17:24.640
Brew!

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:26.600
Brew!

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:38.890
What are you saying?

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:40.530
Your upperclassmen in 
the livestock department

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:42.230
made all this for you first-years!

00:17:43.350 --> 00:17:45.110
Everyone get inside the lecture hall!

00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:47.330
Instructors, please 
notify the hospital!

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:49.330
It's O-157.

00:17:58.830 --> 00:18:02.500
Fortunately, nobody had begun eating,

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:04.220
so I don't think it's serious.

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:06.660
But the instructors should caution 
the students to be alert

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:08.650
until the incubation period has passed.

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:11.590
Any students who haven't 
been seen by a doctor yet,

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:12.800
please raise your hands.

00:18:13.510 --> 00:18:15.940
Don't remove the sticker on your chest.

00:18:17.420 --> 00:18:18.950
Sawaki-kun.

00:18:19.350 --> 00:18:20.660
That was a good catch.

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:22.690
It was the dressing.

00:18:22.690 --> 00:18:24.500
If those things hadn't been in it,

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:26.290
I'd have thought they were 
just ordinary bacteria.

00:18:26.770 --> 00:18:31.290
O-157 can multiply even in 
very acidic environments.

00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:34.940
Someone in the livestock 
department must have

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:37.130
accidentally transferred 
it from a cow or something.

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:41.390
Still, I've never seen a food 
poisoning outbreak like this,

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:43.560
with no victims at all.

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:47.380
But did you really have to speak up?

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:52.900
You're the hot topic among all 
the instructors and first-years.

00:18:53.970 --> 00:18:57.320
I would rather you had avoided 
doing anything that could

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:59.700
risk everyone finding 
out about your ability.

00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:01.370
Professor...

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:02.940
What are you saying?

00:19:04.090 --> 00:19:08.080
Well, this time I convinced them 
that I told you to say it.

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:11.320
Wait a minute, Professor...

00:19:11.320 --> 00:19:15.370
Are you saying I shouldn't 
have... said anything?

00:19:19.460 --> 00:19:20.610
Sawaki!

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:29.420
Sawaki, are you okay?

00:19:29.420 --> 00:19:30.870
Hang in there!

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:31.830
Why did this happen?

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:33.730
You hadn't eaten the curry yet, right?

00:19:35.390 --> 00:19:37.860
I told you, it's just a minor 
stomachache that started this morning...

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:42.180
No, this could be a symptom 
of food poisoning.

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:43.160
We should run tests.

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:45.120
No, it really is just a stomachache...

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:47.910
Now that's what I call applied study.

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:49.430
No, I told you...

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:51.770
I don't mind if he stays here tonight.

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.590
Influenza Virus

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:03.430
No! Hospitals are full of germs!

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:27.390
Moyashimon

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:27.390
Episode 4

00:21:25.520 --> 00:21:27.390
Microbe Theater

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:27.390
Microbe Theater 4!

00:21:32.360 --> 00:21:33.510
Oh, crap!

00:21:33.510 --> 00:21:35.510
Hi! We're O-157!

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:35.790
Yeah!

00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:39.810
We cause food poisoning 
in humans, so, well...

00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:41.900
They don't like us much.

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:44.820
But it's not like we 
have evil intentions.

00:21:45.430 --> 00:21:47.930
You see, it's just that...

00:21:47.930 --> 00:21:51.210
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:54.980
Microbes never think about humans.

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:56.170
That's right, we're called...

00:21:56.170 --> 00:21:58.290
E. coli!

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:58.810
E. coli

00:21:59.230 --> 00:22:02.840
Do you know why E. coli 
are called E. coli?

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:05.140
Because we're found in 
the colon, of course.

00:22:05.140 --> 00:22:08.590
But you know, humans hate us.

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:11.280
No, no! Scientists can 
reassemble our genes

00:22:11.280 --> 00:22:14.020
to create scientific 
materials that are very

00:22:14.020 --> 00:22:15.450
useful in all kinds of research.

00:22:15.450 --> 00:22:18.000
We're doing a lot for the world!

00:22:18.760 --> 00:22:21.150
Yeah, we're so amazing and yet...

00:22:21.150 --> 00:22:23.640
Humans just don't understand.

00:22:23.640 --> 00:22:24.800
Yeah...

00:22:24.880 --> 00:22:29.910
In Microbe Theater 
Episode 5,

00:22:24.880 --> 00:22:29.910
We'll Do the Brewing.

00:22:29.910 --> 00:22:36.160
Next Week: 
"Horrors! The Microbe Monster"

00:22:30.260 --> 00:22:32.240
Sawaki-kun, what did you say you saw?

00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:34.560
What? A microbe monster?
